<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pellegrino Rossi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1787">1787</a>–<a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pellegrino Rossi was an Italian-born economist, jurist and politician who taught in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and served as French ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Appointed chief minister of the Papal States by Pius IX in 1848, he was stabbed to death in November 1848 on the steps of the parliament, prompting the pope's flight to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> of 1849.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pellegrino-rossi.jpg" alt="Pellegrino Rossi" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bridi. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rossi_bridi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
